e just enough  self-awareness to understand to not let  this overtake his writing he seems to be  a very technically minded writer and  what I  say that what I mean is he has a lot of  focus on the little details of exactly  you know the the intricacies of how this  piece of equipment works how this game  works how this society works the nuts  and bolts little technical details very  much come through his writing as being  the thing that he is most interested in  and in the hands of a less self-aware  writer that could lead to something that  I personally wouldn't enjoy because I  don't like getting bogged down in  technical details I like to get the gist  of what's going on and have more of a  focus on the forward momentum and the  emotionality of the story and this story  is not devoid of those things because  E&amp;M Bank seems to know well enough that  as much as there is a lot of technical  details he doesn't forget to move the  story forward  and I actually was nervous going into  this because the the patronize er who  commissioned me for this actually  directed me to a blog post that Iain M  banks I wrote some time ago basically  describing the culture the history of it  and how the society works and I was  advised to read that before reading the  book and I tried I got about two  paragraphs and I'm like I can't read  this and it made me very very very  nervous because I was afraid that that  blog entry was going to be  representative of the book but it's not  that blog entry was essentially just a  just an encyclopedic history of how the  culture works how it functions and I  just I can't absorb information like  that my brain checks out very quickly I  like to take in that information in  context through character interactions  like a little bit of exposition where  it's necessary but largely just to pick  up how it works and because that's how I  took in this story also be aware that if  I say anything wrong about how the  culture works as a society it's p